= Inauguration

The new president takes the oath. Millions of people will march the next day. Within weeks, the administration issues a sweeping travel restriction, fires officials, and tests the boundaries of presidential power. The party's task is no longer to win a campaign but to defend the structure of the republic.

- @resist: Total resistance.
- @selective: Selective opposition.
- @legal: Lawyer up and fight in court.

@resist
subtitle: Energy, but little room for deals.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 6; prog_strength += 3; mod_dissent += 2; far_left += 1

We oppose, loudly and constantly. Our base loves it.

@selective
subtitle: Hold the line where the republic is at stake.
on-arrival: stability += 3; media_trust += 2; enthusiasm += 2; mod_dissent -= 2

We pick our fights. Some on our side call it weakness. Others call it strategy.

@legal
subtitle: The institutional road.
on-arrival: stability += 4; funds -= 1 if funds > 0; media_trust += 1

Attorneys general sue; courts block some actions and permit others.
